From: the jellyfin-ffmpeg contributors
Subject: fix dummy hw frame missing hw frames ctx
Origin: https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg/blob/v8.1.3-2/debian/patches/0068-fix-dummy-hw-frame-missing-hw-frames-ctx.patch

The stand-in frame ffmpeg gives an encoder whose filter graph produced
nothing carries the hardware frames context a hardware encoder needs.

Rebased onto FFmpeg 9.0.2: the same change, at 9.0.2's line numbers.

From jellyfin-ffmpeg 8.1.3-2, where the patch has no header: its authors
are in that repository's history. Under FFmpeg's licence, as the files
it changes.
---
diff --git a/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c b/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c
@@ -2653,10 +2653,21 @@ static int close_output(OutputFilterPriv
     if (!fgt->got_frame) {
         AVFrame *frame = fgt->frame;
         FrameData *fd;
+        const AVPixFmtDescriptor *ofp_fmt_desc;
 
         frame->time_base   = ofp->tb_out;
         frame->format      = ofp->format;
 
+        ofp_fmt_desc = av_pix_fmt_desc_get(ofp->format);
+        // a dummy frame with HW pixel format requires a valid hw_frames_ctx
+        if (ofp_fmt_desc->flags & AV_PIX_FMT_FLAG_HWACCEL) {
+            AVFilterContext *sink = ofp->ofilter.filter;
+            AVBufferRef *hwfc = av_buffersink_get_hw_frames_ctx(sink);
+            ret = av_buffer_replace(&frame->hw_frames_ctx, hwfc);
+            if (ret < 0)
+                return ret;
+        }
+
         frame->width               = ofp->width;
         frame->height              = ofp->height;
         frame->sample_aspect_ratio = ofp->sample_aspect_ratio;
